2.2   Furthermore, in terms of section 1(1) of the Banks Act, an ‘employee in charge of a
      risk management function’, in relation to a bank, is defined as:
             …that employee of the bank who is ultimately responsible for the management of one
             or more of the following types of risk to which the bank is exposed, namely –

             (a) solvency risk;
             (b) liquidity risk;
             (c) credit risk;
             (d) currency risk;
             (e) market risk (position risk);
             (f) interest rate risk;
             (g) counterparty risk;
             (h) technological risk;
             (i) operational risk;
             (j) compliance risk; or
             (k) any other risk regarded as material by that bank.
